' SproutStudio architecture, high level.
' Three diagrams in one file: use the preview's diagram switcher to move between them.
'   1. Layers: what lives where and who may depend on whom.
'   2. Ownership: which objects exist at runtime and who creates them.
'   3. Flow: what happens when you type in the editor.

@startuml layers
title SproutStudio · 1. Layers (arrows = "may use")
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangleRoundCorner 8
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 45

rectangle "**app**\nMain · AppGraph (wires everything by hand) · WindowManager" as app #EEF5FF

rectangle "**features**  (MVVM: one ViewModel + its Composables per feature)\nworkspace · document · editor · preview · problems · explorer\ngit · templates · palette · quickpreview" as features #F1FBEF

rectangle "**ui/designsystem**\nTheme · Components · icons" as ds #FFF8E8
rectangle "**platform**\nmacOS: dialogs · Trash · Finder · clipboard" as platform #F5F0FF

rectangle "**services**  (IO + concurrency, never UI state)\nrender · git · files · persistence" as services #FFF1F1

rectangle "**domain**  (pure Kotlin: no Compose, no IO)\nPlantUML language · completion · templates · folding · syntax\nfind & replace · LineDiff" as domain #F4F4F4

rectangle "**core**  (usable by every layer)\nAppDispatchers · LatestWinsQueue · SettingsStore · ViewModel base" as core #EAF7F7

app -down-> features
features -down-> ds
features -down-> platform
features -down-> services
services -down-> domain
domain -down[hidden]-> core

note right of features
  Views draw state and call ViewModel methods.
  ViewModels change state on Main only and never
  build user text (views do it: ready for i18n).
end note

note right of services
  Behind interfaces (RenderService, GitService...),
  so ViewModel tests use fakes.
  Errors are typed: GitError, FileError, RenderError.
end note

legend bottom
  features may also use domain directly.
  ArchitectureTest enforces these arrows and one public class per file.
endlegend
@enduml

@startuml ownership
title SproutStudio · 2. Who owns what at runtime
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangleRoundCorner 8
top to bottom direction

rectangle "AppGraph  (one per app, built in Main)" as graph #EEF5FF {
  rectangle "Settings\ntheme · layout · diagram\nautosave · recents" as settings
  rectangle "RenderService\none PlantUML thread" as render
  rectangle "GitService" as git
  rectangle "DocumentStore\nonly writer to disk" as store
  rectangle "ProjectFiles" as files
  rectangle "Platform" as platform
  rectangle "WindowManager" as wm
}

rectangle "Project window  (one per window)" as win #F1FBEF {
  rectangle "WorkspaceViewModel\nits scope lives as long as the window" as wvm {
    rectangle "Document\none per tab" as doc
    rectangle "GitViewModel" as gvm
  }
  rectangle "Composables\nProjectWindow · Workspace · panels" as views
  rectangle "PreviewViewModel\none per visible preview,\nclosed when the preview leaves" as pvm
}

wm -down-> win : opens / closes
graph .down.> wvm : WorkspaceDeps
views -right-> wvm : read state,\ncall methods
views -down-> pvm : creates
pvm ..> doc : reads text
pvm --> render
gvm --> git
wvm --> files
wvm --> store

note bottom of win
  Closing the window cancels the WorkspaceViewModel scope,
  so every job of that window stops. Closing a panel does not:
  a commit or a save keeps going.
end note
@enduml

@startuml flow
title SproutStudio · 3. What happens when you type
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

actor User
participant "CodeEditor\n(View)" as editor
participant "Document" as doc
participant "PreviewViewModel" as pvm
participant "RenderService" as render
participant "LatestWinsQueue\n(one PlantUML thread)" as queue
participant "AutoSaver" as autosave
participant "DocumentStore" as store

User -> editor : types
editor -> doc : new text

par preview
  doc -> pvm : text changed
  pvm -> pvm : wait 300 ms (debounce);\na new keystroke restarts it
  pvm -> render : problems(text)
  render -> queue : submit(URGENT, key = problems of this doc)
  queue --> pvm : List<Problem>
  pvm --> editor : red lines + Problems panel
  pvm -> render : preview(text)
  render -> queue : submit(NORMAL, key = preview of this doc)
  note right of queue
    A newer request with the same key
    replaces the one still waiting, so
    stale renders never pile up.
    Gallery thumbnails run as BACKGROUND
    and never delay the preview.
  end note
  queue --> pvm : RenderResult (PNG)
  pvm --> editor : preview image
else autosave
  doc -> autosave : dirty
  autosave -> store : write(file, text)
  note right of store
    Runs on IO, one lock per file.
    Save, rollback, rename and move
    go through here too.
  end note
end
@enduml
